{:steps
 [{:name "decompile",
   :type :delegate,
   :temperature 0,
   :target "lambda-decompiler",
   :skills ["lambda-compiler"],
   :prompt-string
   {:type :template,
    :text "Decompile the lambda expression to prose:\n{{lambda}}",
    :vars {"lambda" {:from :workflow-input, :path [:input]}}},
   :context [{:type :source, :from :workflow-original}]}
  {:name "compile",
   :type :delegate,
   :temperature 0,
   :target "lambda-compiler",
   :skills ["lambda-compiler"],
   :prompt-string
   {:type :template,
    :text "Compile a lambda for:\n{{prose}}",
    :vars {"prose" {:from {:step "decompile", :yield :text}}}},
   :context
   [{:type :source, :from :workflow-original}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "decompile", :yield :text}}]}
  {:name "compare",
   :type :session,
   :tools ["read" "bash"],
   :skills ["lambda-compiler"],
   :contributions
   [{:type :source, :from :workflow-original}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "decompile", :yield :text}}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "compile", :yield :text}}
    {:type :template,
     :text
     "Compare the newly compiled lambda with the previous iteration's lambda.\n\nPrevious lambda (input to this cycle's decompile step):\n{{previous}}\n\nNewly compiled lambda:\n{{current}}\n\nDetermine whether these two lambda expressions are structurally equivalent — same semantics, same structure, same symbols. Minor whitespace or formatting differences do not count as changes.\n\nFirst, write a brief one-sentence summary of what changed (or that nothing changed).\n\nThen end your reply with the routing marker on its own final line, written verbatim as exactly one of these two lines, with no leading dash, bullet, indentation, quote, or any trailing text:\n\nFIXPOINT_ROUTE: FIXED\n\nFIXPOINT_ROUTE: CHANGED\n\nUse FIXED if the two lambdas are equivalent, or CHANGED if they differ. The marker must appear exactly once, start at the very first column of the line (no characters before FIXPOINT_ROUTE), have exactly one space after the colon, and contain only the single token FIXED or CHANGED.",
     :vars
     {"previous" {:from :workflow-input, :path [:input]},
      "current" {:from {:step "compile", :yield :text}}}}],
   :judge
   {:type :invoke,
    :operation "workflow/exact-marker-routing",
    :args
    {:text {:from {:step "compare", :output :final-llm-reply}},
     :marker-label "FIXPOINT_ROUTE",
     :allowed-routes ["FIXED" "CHANGED"]}},
   :on
   {"FIXED" {:goto "report"},
    "CHANGED" {:goto "iterate-decompile", :max-iterations 5, :on-max-iterations "diagnose-churn"}}}
  {:name "iterate-decompile",
   :type :delegate,
   :temperature 0,
   :target "lambda-decompiler",
   :skills ["lambda-compiler"],
   :prompt-string
   {:type :template,
    :text "Decompile the lambda expression to prose:\n{{lambda}}",
    :vars {"lambda" {:from {:step "compile", :yield :text}}}},
   :context [{:type :source, :from :workflow-original}]}
  {:name "iterate-compile",
   :type :delegate,
   :temperature 0,
   :target "lambda-compiler",
   :skills ["lambda-compiler"],
   :prompt-string
   {:type :template,
    :text "Compile a lambda for:\n{{prose}}",
    :vars {"prose" {:from {:step "iterate-decompile", :yield :text}}}},
   :context
   [{:type :source, :from :workflow-original}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "iterate-decompile", :yield :text}}]}
  {:name "iterate-compare",
   :type :session,
   :tools ["read" "bash"],
   :skills ["lambda-compiler"],
   :contributions
   [{:type :source, :from :workflow-original}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "iterate-decompile", :yield :text}}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "iterate-compile", :yield :text}}
    {:type :template,
     :text
     "Compare the newly compiled lambda with the previous iteration's lambda.\n\nPrevious lambda (input to this cycle's decompile step):\n{{previous}}\n\nNewly compiled lambda:\n{{current}}\n\nDetermine whether these two lambda expressions are structurally equivalent — same semantics, same structure, same symbols. Minor whitespace or formatting differences do not count as changes.\n\nFirst, write a brief one-sentence summary of what changed (or that nothing changed).\n\nThen end your reply with the routing marker on its own final line, written verbatim as exactly one of these two lines, with no leading dash, bullet, indentation, quote, or any trailing text:\n\nFIXPOINT_ROUTE: FIXED\n\nFIXPOINT_ROUTE: CHANGED\n\nUse FIXED if the two lambdas are equivalent, or CHANGED if they differ. The marker must appear exactly once, start at the very first column of the line (no characters before FIXPOINT_ROUTE), have exactly one space after the colon, and contain only the single token FIXED or CHANGED.",
     :vars
     {"previous" {:from {:step "compile", :yield :text}},
      "current" {:from {:step "iterate-compile", :yield :text}}}}],
   :judge
   {:type :invoke,
    :operation "workflow/exact-marker-routing",
    :args
    {:text {:from {:step "iterate-compare", :output :final-llm-reply}},
     :marker-label "FIXPOINT_ROUTE",
     :allowed-routes ["FIXED" "CHANGED"]}},
   :on
   {"FIXED" {:goto "report"},
    "CHANGED" {:goto "iterate-decompile", :max-iterations 5, :on-max-iterations "diagnose-churn"}}}

  {:name "diagnose-churn",
   :type :session,
   :tools ["read" "bash"],
   :skills ["lambda-compiler"],
   :contributions
   [{:type :source, :from :workflow-original}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "iterate-decompile", :yield :text}}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "iterate-compile", :yield :text}}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "iterate-compare", :output :final-llm-reply}}
    {:type :template,
     :text
     "Produce a non-convergence report for the lambda fixpoint workflow.

The workflow exhausted its iteration limit because decompile/recompile cycles kept changing the lambda instead of reaching a stable fixpoint.

## Original Lambda
{{original}}

## Latest Decompiled Prose
{{latest_prose}}

## Latest Compiled Lambda
{{latest_lambda}}

## Latest Comparison
{{latest_comparison}}

Your task:
1. State clearly that no fixpoint was reached within the configured iteration limit.
2. Identify the symbols, names, operators, or structural forms that appear to be churning between iterations.
3. Identify the underlying concepts or semantic distinctions that appear unstable (for example: recursion vs iteration, self/other boundaries, order vs entropy, implementation detail vs intent).
4. For each churn item, explain the likely cause of non-convergence and what constraint or wording would likely stabilize it.
5. If the evidence is insufficient for a confident diagnosis, say what comparison evidence is missing instead of guessing.

Format your output as:

## No Fixpoint Reached
<one-sentence summary>

## Churning Symbols / Forms
- `<symbol-or-form>` — <how it is changing and why it matters>

## Churning Concepts
- `<concept>` — <unstable interpretation and likely stabilizing constraint>

## Stabilization Advice
<minimal advice for making the lambda converge>",
     :vars
     {"original" {:from :workflow-input, :path [:input]},
      "latest_prose" {:from {:step "iterate-decompile", :yield :text}},
      "latest_lambda" {:from {:step "iterate-compile", :yield :text}},
      "latest_comparison" {:from {:step "iterate-compare", :output :final-llm-reply}}}}],
   :judge
   {:type :invoke,
    :operation "workflow/constant-routing",
    :args {:route "DONE"}},
   :on {"DONE" {:goto :done}}}
  {:name "report",
   :type :session,
   :tools ["read" "bash"],
   :skills ["lambda-compiler"],
   :contributions
   [{:type :source, :from :workflow-original}
    {:type :source, :from {:step "iterate-compile", :yield :text}}
    {:type :template,
     :text
     "Produce the final fixpoint report.\n\nThe lambda expression has reached a stable form after iterative decompile/recompile cycles.\n\n## Original Lambda\n{{original}}\n\n## Final Compiled Lambda\n{{compiled}}\n\nYour task:\n1. Show the final compiled lambda expression (the fixpoint form).\n2. Decompile that fixpoint lambda into clear, readable prose.\n3. If the fixpoint differs from the original, briefly note what was refined.\n\nFormat your output as:\n\n## Fixpoint Lambda\n<the stable lambda>\n\n## Decompiled\n<prose equivalent>\n\n## Delta\n<what changed from original, or \"No changes — original was already at fixpoint\">",
     :vars
     {"original" {:from :workflow-input, :path [:input]},
      "compiled" {:from {:step "iterate-compile", :yield :text}}}}]}],
 :name "lambda-fixpoint",
 :description
 "Iterate a lambda expression to a fixpoint by decompiling and recompiling until stable"}
